            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Hindi for trickery, then the Hindi for to lure."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: उपन्यास",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "उपन्यास — upanyās — \"a novel\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "मीरा ने छुट्टी में एक लंबा उपन्यास पढ़ा। Mīrā ne chuṭṭī meṁ ek lambā upanyās paṛhā. Mira read a long novel during the holidays."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Masculine."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "उपन्यास (upanyās) is Sanskrit upanyāsa, \"a placing near; a statement\" (Monier-Williams). Modern Hindi uses it for a novel; the dictionary gives only the older senses."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling what happened."
